LESSON = "st3-l06-global-frameworks-conventions"
SECTIONS = {s: f"st3-l06-global-biodiversity-governance-l6-{s}" for s in "abcd"}

facts = [
 ("a-f022","a","A convention and a protocol are separate legal instruments. A State becomes bound through the applicable consent procedure; joining a parent convention does not automatically make it Party to every protocol under it.","Convention, protocol వేర్వేరు legal instruments. సంబంధిత consent procedure పూర్తయితేనే Stateకు బాధ్యతలు వర్తిస్తాయి; parent conventionలో చేరినంత మాత్రాన దాని ప్రతి protocolకు Party కాదు.",["src-cbd-treaty"]),
 ("a-f023","a","The CBD was adopted and opened for signature on 5 June 1992 and entered into force on 29 December 1993.","CBDను 5 June 1992న adopt చేసి signature కోసం open చేశారు; అది 29 December 1993న అమల్లోకి వచ్చింది.",["src-cbd-treaty"]),
 ("a-f024","a","Cartagena's Advance Informed Agreement procedure applies to specified LMOs intended for intentional introduction into the environment; it does not apply identically to every movement or use of an LMO.","Cartagenaలోని Advance Informed Agreement procedure, environmentలో intentional introduction కోసం ఉద్దేశించిన నిర్దిష్ట LMOsకు వర్తిస్తుంది; ప్రతి LMO movement లేదా useకు ఒకేలా వర్తించదు.",["src-cbd-protocols"]),
 ("a-f025","a","The Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol entered into force on 5 March 2018. It concerns response measures for biodiversity damage from LMOs originating in transboundary movement, not general ABS.","Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol 5 March 2018న అమల్లోకి వచ్చింది. ఇది transboundary movement నుంచి వచ్చిన LMOs వల్ల biodiversity damageకు response measures గురించి; general ABS గురించి కాదు.",["src-cbd-protocols"]),
 ("b-f012","b","CITES Appendix I does not prohibit every movement. Primarily commercial trade in wild-sourced specimens is generally prohibited, while exceptional non-commercial trade is controlled by import and export permits; qualifying captive-bred or artificially propagated commercial specimens may be treated under Appendix-II rules.","CITES Appendix I ప్రతి movementను నిషేధించదు. Wild-sourced specimens యొక్క primarily commercial trade సాధారణంగా నిషేధం; exceptional non-commercial tradeకు import, export permits అవసరం. అర్హత గల captive-bred లేదా artificially propagated commercial specimensకు Appendix-II rules వర్తించవచ్చు.",["src-cites-official"]),
 ("b-f013","b","For CITES Appendix III, export from the Party that listed the species requires an export permit; export from another range State requires a certificate of origin, and re-export requires a re-export certificate.","CITES Appendix IIIలో speciesను list చేసిన Party నుంచి exportకు export permit అవసరం; మరో range State నుంచి exportకు certificate of origin, re-exportకు re-export certificate అవసరం.",["src-cites-official"]),
 ("b-f014","b","CITES introduction from the sea means bringing into a State a specimen taken in a marine area beyond any State's jurisdiction. Its certificate and NDF rules apply to Appendices I and II, not Appendix III.","CITESలో introduction from the sea అంటే ఏ State jurisdictionకూ చెందని marine area నుంచి తీసిన specimenను ఒక Stateలోకి తేవడం. దీనికి సంబంధించిన certificate, NDF rules Appendices I, IIకు వర్తిస్తాయి; Appendix IIIకు కాదు.",["src-cites-official"]),
 ("b-f015","b","The IUCN Red List assesses extinction risk, CITES Appendices regulate international trade, and India's Wild Life (Protection) Act Schedules determine domestic legal protection. A change in one system does not automatically change the others.","IUCN Red List extinction riskను assess చేస్తుంది; CITES Appendices international tradeను regulate చేస్తాయి; India's Wild Life (Protection) Act Schedules domestic legal protectionను నిర్ణయిస్తాయి. ఒక systemలో change వచ్చినంత మాత్రాన మిగతావి automaticగా మారవు.",["src-cites-official"]),
 ("c-f010","c","A biosphere reserve has three connected functions: conservation, sustainable development, and logistic support through research, monitoring, education and training. Core, buffer and transition zones support these functions in different ways.","Biosphere reserveకు మూడు connected functions ఉన్నాయి: conservation, sustainable development, research-monitoring-education-training ద్వారా logistic support. Core, buffer, transition zones ఈ functionsను వేర్వేరు విధాలుగా support చేస్తాయి.",["src-unesco-mab-biosphere-reserves"]),
 ("c-f011","c","The Plant Treaty Multilateral System covers 64 Annex-I food crops and forages and uses the Standard Material Transfer Agreement. Farmers' Rights include traditional knowledge, benefit-sharing and participation in decisions, with implementation resting on national governments under national law.","Plant Treaty Multilateral System Annex Iలోని 64 food crops, foragesను cover చేసి Standard Material Transfer Agreementను ఉపయోగిస్తుంది. Farmers' Rightsలో traditional knowledge, benefit-sharing, decisionsలో participation ఉంటాయి; national law ప్రకారం implementation national governments బాధ్యత.",["src-fao-itpgrfa-overview"]),
 ("d-f008","d","India released its updated NBSAP for 2024–2030 at CBD COP16 in October 2024. It aligns with the KMGBF's four goals and 23 targets and sets 23 National Biodiversity Targets; aligned global and national targets are not identical legal provisions.","India తన updated NBSAP 2024–2030ను October 2024లో CBD COP16 వద్ద విడుదల చేసింది. ఇది KMGBFలోని four goals, 23 targetsతో align అయి 23 National Biodiversity Targetsను నిర్దేశిస్తుంది; aligned global, national targets ఒకే legal provisions కావు.",["src-pib-india-nbsap-2024"]),
 ("d-f009","d","India submitted its Seventh CBD National Report on 26 February 2026 under CBD Article 26, using 142 national indicators mapped to 23 National Biodiversity Targets. It submitted its first Nagoya Protocol implementation report on 27 February 2026 under Protocol Article 29; the reports have different legal bases and subjects.","India 23 National Biodiversity Targetsకు map చేసిన 142 national indicatorsతో Seventh CBD National Reportను CBD Article 26 కింద 26 February 2026న submit చేసింది. First Nagoya Protocol implementation reportను Protocol Article 29 కింద 27 February 2026న submit చేసింది; రెండింటి legal bases, subjects వేరు.",["src-pib-india-biodiversity-reports-2026"]),
]

def opts(a,b,c,d): return {"a":a,"b":b,"c":c,"d":d}
questions = [
 ("a-q049","a-f022","Which inference about treaty participation is correct?","Treaty participation గురించి సరైన inference ఏది?",opts("Joining a convention does not automatically join every protocol under it.","Every protocol automatically binds all convention Parties.","A protocol is only a non-legal press note.","Signature always equals ratification."),opts("Conventionలో చేరితే దాని ప్రతి protocolలో automaticగా చేరరు.","Convention Parties అందరికీ ప్రతి protocol automaticగా వర్తిస్తుంది.","Protocol అనేది non-legal press note మాత్రమే.","Signature ఎప్పుడూ ratificationతో సమానం."),"a","M","concept-application","Consent to be bound is assessed separately for the convention and each protocol.","Convention, ప్రతి protocolకు consent to be boundను వేరుగా చూడాలి."),
 ("a-q050","a-f022","Assertion (A): A CBD Party need not automatically be a Party to the Nagoya Protocol. Reason (R): A protocol is a separate instrument with its own procedure for consent to be bound.","Assertion (A): CBD Party automaticగా Nagoya Protocol Party కావాల్సిన అవసరం లేదు. Reason (R): Protocol వేరే instrument; consent to be boundకు దాని సొంత procedure ఉంటుంది.",opts("Both A and R are true, and R explains A.","Both are true, but R does not explain A.","A is true, but R is false.","A is false, but R is true."),opts("A, R రెండూ నిజం; R, Aను వివరిస్తుంది.","రెండూ నిజం; R, Aను వివరించదు.","A నిజం; R తప్పు.","A తప్పు; R నిజం."),"a","H","assertion-reason","Both are true; separate consent explains the distinction.","రెండూ నిజం; separate consent ఈ distinctionను వివరిస్తుంది."),
 ("a-q051","a-f023","Choose the correct CBD chronology.","సరైన CBD chronologyను ఎంచుకోండి.",opts("Entered force in 1992; adopted in 1993","Adopted/opened for signature on 5 June 1992; entered force on 29 December 1993","Adopted in 1971; entered force in 1975","Adopted and entered force on the same day in 1992"),opts("1992లో force; 1993లో adopt","5 June 1992న adopt/signature కోసం open; 29 December 1993న force","1971లో adopt; 1975లో force","1992లో ఒకే రోజు adopt, force"),"b","E","sequence","Adoption/signature opening preceded entry into force.","Adoption/signature opening తరువాత entry into force వచ్చింది."),
 ("a-q052","a-f024","A shipment contains an LMO intended only for direct food processing. Which caution is most accurate?","ఒక LMO direct food processingకే ఉద్దేశించబడింది. సరైన caution ఏది?",opts("AIA always applies identically to every LMO use.","Cartagena never regulates transboundary LMOs.","AIA is designed for specified LMOs intentionally introduced into the environment, so it should not be assumed identical for this use.","The Nagoya ABS procedure replaces Cartagena AIA."),opts("ప్రతి LMO useకు AIA ఒకేలా వర్తిస్తుంది.","Cartagena transboundary LMOsను regulate చేయదు.","AIA, environmentలో intentional introduction కోసం specified LMOsకు; ఈ useకు identical అని assume చేయకూడదు.","Nagoya ABS procedure Cartagena AIAను replace చేస్తుంది."),"c","H","application-scenario","AIA has a defined scope and is not a universal procedure for all LMO movements.","AIAకు defined scope ఉంది; అన్ని LMO movementsకు universal procedure కాదు."),
 ("a-q053","a-f025","Match the instrument with its principal focus: 1. Nagoya Protocol 2. Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol; P. ABS Q. LMO damage response measures.","Instrumentను principal focusతో match చేయండి: 1. Nagoya Protocol 2. Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol; P. ABS Q. LMO damage response measures.",opts("1-Q, 2-P","1-P, 2-P","1-Q, 2-Q","1-P, 2-Q"),opts("1-Q, 2-P","1-P, 2-P","1-Q, 2-Q","1-P, 2-Q"),"d","M","match","Nagoya concerns ABS; the Supplementary Protocol concerns liability/redress response measures for LMO damage.","Nagoya ABS గురించి; Supplementary Protocol LMO damage response measures గురించి."),
 ("b-q025","b-f012","Which statement about CITES Appendix I is correct?","CITES Appendix I గురించి సరైన statement ఏది?",opts("Every movement of every specimen is absolutely prohibited.","Wild-sourced primarily commercial trade is generally prohibited, but controlled exceptions and special captive-bred rules exist.","It contains only species that are not threatened.","It never requires an import permit."),opts("ప్రతి specimen ప్రతి movement పూర్తిగా prohibited.","Wild-sourced primarily commercial trade సాధారణంగా prohibited; controlled exceptions, special captive-bred rules ఉన్నాయి.","Threatened కాని species మాత్రమే ఉంటాయి.","Import permit ఎప్పుడూ అవసరం లేదు."),"b","M","concept","Appendix I is highly restrictive, not an absolute ban on every movement.","Appendix I చాలా restrictive; ప్రతి movementపై absolute ban కాదు."),
 ("b-q026","b-f013","A specimen of an Appendix-III species is exported from a range State other than the Party that listed it. Which document is normally required?","Appendix-III species specimenను list చేసిన Party కాకుండా మరో range State export చేస్తోంది. సాధారణంగా ఏ document అవసరం?",opts("Certificate of origin","Appendix-I import permit only","NBSAP","Montreux certificate"),opts("Certificate of origin","Appendix-I import permit మాత్రమే","NBSAP","Montreux certificate"),"a","E","factual-application","A non-listing range State supplies a certificate of origin.","Non-listing range State certificate of origin ఇస్తుంది."),
 ("b-q027","b-f014","Under CITES, 'introduction from the sea' refers to:","CITESలో 'introduction from the sea' అంటే:",opts("Any coastal export between neighbouring States","Releasing a captive animal into a river","Bringing into a State a specimen taken beyond every State's marine jurisdiction","Listing a wetland under Ramsar"),opts("Neighbouring States మధ్య ఏ coastal export అయినా","Captive animalను riverలో release చేయడం","ఏ State marine jurisdictionకూ చెందని areaలో తీసిన specimenను Stateలోకి తేవడం","Wetlandను Ramsar కింద list చేయడం"),"c","E","definition","The term concerns specimens taken in marine areas beyond national jurisdiction.","ఈ term national jurisdictionకు బయట marine areaలో తీసిన specimensకు సంబంధించినది."),
 ("b-q028","b-f015","Match correctly: 1. IUCN Red List 2. CITES Appendices 3. Indian wildlife-law Schedules; P. extinction risk Q. international-trade control R. domestic legal protection.","సరిగా match చేయండి: 1. IUCN Red List 2. CITES Appendices 3. Indian wildlife-law Schedules; P. extinction risk Q. international-trade control R. domestic legal protection.",opts("1-Q, 2-P, 3-R","1-R, 2-Q, 3-P","1-P, 2-R, 3-Q","1-P, 2-Q, 3-R"),opts("1-Q, 2-P, 3-R","1-R, 2-Q, 3-P","1-P, 2-R, 3-Q","1-P, 2-Q, 3-R"),"d","M","match","The systems assess risk, regulate international trade and provide domestic legal protection respectively.","ఈ systems వరుసగా risk assess చేస్తాయి, international trade regulate చేస్తాయి, domestic legal protection ఇస్తాయి."),
 ("c-q017","c-f010","Which set gives the three connected functions of a biosphere reserve?","Biosphere reserve మూడు connected functions ఏ setలో ఉన్నాయి?",opts("Trade, policing, taxation","Conservation, sustainable development, logistic support","Mining, navigation, customs","Ratification, accession, reservation"),opts("Trade, policing, taxation","Conservation, sustainable development, logistic support","Mining, navigation, customs","Ratification, accession, reservation"),"b","E","fact","MAB links conservation and development with research, monitoring, education and training support.","MAB conservation, developmentను research, monitoring, education, training supportతో link చేస్తుంది."),
 ("c-q018","c-f010","A programme supports sustainable livelihoods and stakeholder cooperation around a biosphere reserve. Which zone best fits?","Biosphere reserve చుట్టూ sustainable livelihoods, stakeholder cooperationకు programme support చేస్తోంది. ఏ zone సరిపోతుంది?",opts("Core zone","World Heritage danger list","Transition zone","CITES Appendix I"),opts("Core zone","World Heritage danger list","Transition zone","CITES Appendix I"),"c","M","application-scenario","The transition zone emphasizes cooperation and sustainable livelihoods.","Transition zone cooperation, sustainable livelihoodsపై emphasis ఇస్తుంది."),
 ("c-q019","c-f011","Which pairing is correct under the Plant Treaty?","Plant Treaty కింద సరైన pairing ఏది?",opts("64 Annex-I crops/forages — Multilateral System using SMTA","All wild species — CITES import permits","Wetlands — Montreux listing","Migratory species — CMS MoU only"),opts("64 Annex-I crops/forages — SMTA ఉపయోగించే Multilateral System","అన్ని wild species — CITES import permits","Wetlands — Montreux listing","Migratory species — CMS MoU మాత్రమే"),"a","M","match","The Multilateral System uses the Standard Material Transfer Agreement for Annex-I material.","Annex-I material కోసం Multilateral System Standard Material Transfer Agreementను ఉపయోగిస్తుంది."),
 ("c-q020","c-f011","Assertion (A): Farmers' Rights under the Plant Treaty include participation in relevant decision-making. Reason (R): Their implementation rests with national governments under national law.","Assertion (A): Plant Treatyలో Farmers' Rights relevant decision-makingలో participationను include చేస్తాయి. Reason (R): వాటి implementation national law కింద national governmentsపై ఉంటుంది.",opts("A is false, but R is true.","Both are true, but R does not explain why participation is itself a listed element.","A is true, but R is false.","Both are false."),opts("A తప్పు; R నిజం.","రెండూ నిజం; కానీ participation listed element ఎందుకో R వివరించదు.","A నిజం; R తప్పు.","రెండూ తప్పు."),"b","H","assertion-reason","Both statements are true, but they state different aspects of Farmers' Rights.","రెండు statements నిజం; Farmers' Rightsలో వేర్వేరు aspectsను చెబుతున్నాయి."),
 ("d-q022","d-f008","India's updated NBSAP for 2024–2030 contains:","India updated NBSAP 2024–2030లో ఉన్నవి:",opts("Four national targets only","Twenty Aichi targets copied unchanged","Thirty legally identical treaty articles","Twenty-three National Biodiversity Targets aligned with, but not legally identical to, the KMGBF"),opts("Four national targets మాత్రమే","Twenty Aichi targets unchangedగా","Thirty identical treaty articles","KMGBFతో aligned అయినా legally identical కాని 23 National Biodiversity Targets"),"d","E","fact","India nationalized the framework through 23 National Biodiversity Targets.","India frameworkను 23 National Biodiversity Targets ద్వారా national contextకు అనుసంధానించింది."),
 ("d-q023","d-f008","A student says India's Target 3 and KMGBF Target 3 must be the same legal provision because they are aligned. Evaluate.","India Target 3, KMGBF Target 3 aligned కాబట్టి ఒకే legal provision అని student అంటాడు. Evaluate చేయండి.",opts("Incorrect: alignment of direction does not make global and national targets legally identical.","Correct: every national target is automatically a treaty article.","Correct: NBSAP replaces the CBD.","Incorrect only because India has no NBSAP."),opts("తప్పు: direction alignment వల్ల global, national targets legally identical కావు.","సరైనది: ప్రతి national target automaticగా treaty article.","సరైనది: NBSAP CBDను replace చేస్తుంది.","Indiaకు NBSAP లేదు కాబట్టి మాత్రమే తప్పు."),"a","H","concept-application","Policy alignment and legal identity are different propositions.","Policy alignment, legal identity వేర్వేరు propositions."),
 ("d-q024","d-f009","Which report–legal basis pair is correct?","సరైన report–legal basis pair ఏది?",opts("Seventh CBD National Report — Nagoya Article 29","First Nagoya implementation report — CBD Article 26","Seventh CBD National Report — CBD Article 26; first Nagoya report — Protocol Article 29","Both reports — BBNJ Article 52"),opts("Seventh CBD National Report — Nagoya Article 29","First Nagoya report — CBD Article 26","Seventh CBD National Report — CBD Article 26; first Nagoya report — Protocol Article 29","రెండు reports — BBNJ Article 52"),"c","M","comparison","The two reports arise under different instruments and provisions.","రెండు reports వేర్వేరు instruments, provisions కింద వస్తాయి."),
 ("d-q025","d-f009","Arrange India's 2026 submissions chronologically: 1. Seventh CBD National Report 2. First Nagoya Protocol implementation report.","India 2026 submissionsను chronologyలో పెట్టండి: 1. Seventh CBD National Report 2. First Nagoya Protocol implementation report.",opts("2 on 26 February, then 1 on 27 February","Both on 26 February","1 on 26 February, then 2 on 27 February","Both on 27 February"),opts("2 — 26 February; తరువాత 1 — 27 February","రెండూ 26 February","1 — 26 February; తరువాత 2 — 27 February","రెండూ 27 February"),"c","M","sequence","The CBD report was submitted one day before the Nagoya report.","CBD report, Nagoya reportకంటే ఒక రోజు ముందు submit అయింది."),
]

fact_rows=[]
for suffix,stream,en,te,sources in facts:
    fid="st3-l06-"+suffix
    fact_rows.append({"lesson_id":LESSON,"section_id":SECTIONS[stream],"id":fid+"-p001","fact_id":fid,"en":en,"te":te,"source_ids":sources})

q_rows=[]
for qid_suffix,fid_suffix,qen,qte,o_en,o_te,key,diff,qtype,xen,xte in questions:
    stream=qid_suffix[0]
    q_rows.append({"id":"st3-l06-"+qid_suffix,"lesson_id":LESSON,"section_id":SECTIONS[stream],"fact_ids":["st3-l06-"+fid_suffix],"question_en":qen,"question_te":qte,"options_en":o_en,"options_te":o_te,"correct_answer":key,"difficulty":diff,"qtype":qtype,"explanation_en":xen,"explanation_te":xte,"review_status":"bilingual_approved"})

def load_jsonl(path): return [json.loads(x) for x in path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if x.strip()]
def write_jsonl(path,rows): path.write_text("".join(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(",",":"))+"\n" for x in rows),encoding="utf-8")

fp=BOOK/"facts.jsonl"; old=load_jsonl(fp); ids={x.get("fact_id") for x in old}; assert not ids.intersection(x["fact_id"] for x in fact_rows); write_jsonl(fp,old+fact_rows)
qp=BOOK/"questions.jsonl"; oldq=load_jsonl(qp); qids={x.get("id") for x in oldq}; assert not qids.intersection(x["id"] for x in q_rows); write_jsonl(qp,oldq+q_rows)

manifest=json.loads((BOOK/"manifest.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8")); lesson=next(x for x in manifest["lessons"] if x["id"]==LESSON)
for s in lesson["sections"]:
    stream=s["id"][-1]
    s["fact_ids"] += [x["fact_id"] for x in fact_rows if x["section_id"]==s["id"]]
    s["mcq_ids"] += [x["id"] for x in q_rows if x["section_id"]==s["id"]]
(BOOK/"manifest.json").write_text(json.dumps(manifest,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+"\n",encoding="utf-8")

mp=BOOK/"section_map.json"; sm=json.loads(mp.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
for sid,e in sm.items():
    if e.get("lesson_id")==LESSON:
        e["fact_ids"] += [x["fact_id"] for x in fact_rows if x["section_id"]==sid]
        e["mcq_ids"] += [x["id"] for x in q_rows if x["section_id"]==sid]
mp.write_text(json.dumps(sm,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+"\n",encoding="utf-8")
print(f"added facts={len(fact_rows)} questions={len(q_rows)}")
